(4996181, 727102, 88204, '<td valign="top">I like the halo light on the background. I find self portraits challenging. I think it may be more impactful if the eyes were looking at the camera.</td>', 'I like the halo light on the background. I find self portraits challenging. I think it may be more impactful if the eyes were looking at the camera.', '2008-10-07 00:26:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996227, 727185, 62357, '<td valign="top">Nice job.....</td>', 'Nice job.....', '2008-10-07 00:53:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996253, 726984, 23002, '<td valign="top">Well I am sure she likely appreciates this shot better than your abstract one. ;)<br/> <br/>From what I can see your hair light is spilling over and catching both her glasses and also just inside her collar causing some hot spots.  The hair light must be almost bare bulb cause it seems a bit hard.<br/> <br/>She is certainly a lovely model and this is a nice shot, but would be better without the situation mentioned earlier. :)<br/> <br/>Good luck.</td>', 'Well I am sure she likely appreciates this shot better than your abstract one. ;) From what I can see your hair light is spilling over and catching both her glasses and also just inside her collar causing some hot spots.  The hair light must be almost bare bulb cause it seems a bit hard. She is certainly a lovely model and this is a nice shot, but would be better without the situation mentioned earlier. :) Good luck.', '2008-10-07 01:12:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996256, 727151, 23002, '<td valign="top">Let me see, no hair and a goatee, Jason?<br/> <br/>the very strong lighting here along with the piercing stare makes me think not of sadness but of anger, like you are thinking about all the trolls voting this image down!<br/> <br/>Seriously though I like it, although I am sure if this challenge was in advanced editing (like it should have been...) you would have then toned down the ear in the left of the frame a bit and the shiny bits on the face.<br/> <br/>Nice work. 7</td>', 'Let me see, no hair and a goatee, Jason? the very strong lighting here along with the piercing stare makes me think not of sadness but of anger, like you are thinking about all the trolls voting this image down! Seriously though I like it, although I am sure if this challenge was in advanced editing (like it should have been...) you would have then toned down the ear in the left of the frame a bit and the shiny bits on the face. Nice work. 7', '2008-10-07 01:15:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996258, 726981, 23002, '<td valign="top">Looks great.  no vote from me.  good luck. :)<br/> <br/>I think your expression really makes this come together.</td>', 'Looks great.  no vote from me.  good luck. :) I think your expression really makes this come together.', '2008-10-07 01:15:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996260, 726942, 23002, '<td valign="top">A wonderful portrait of an older man. :)<br/> <br/>I think because you are including the hands to show the knitting I would have backed off a bit to include a bit more of the arms so it does not look like his hands grow out of his checst.  <br/> <br/>I think perhaps a bit more fill would have been nice too because the dark side of his nose is almost black.<br/> <br/>overall a great shot that really captures some personality, which is what it is all about!</td>', 'A wonderful portrait of an older man. :) I think because you are including the hands to show the knitting I would have backed off a bit to include a bit more of the arms so it does not look like his hands grow out of his checst.   I think perhaps a bit more fill would have been nice too because the dark side of his nose is almost black. overall a great shot that really captures some personality, which is what it is all about!', '2008-10-07 01:18:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996261, 726399, 23002, '<td valign="top">aka young death?<br/> <br/>Great except for the finger touching his nose so it looks kind of odd, and the harsh shadow to the viewing left of his hand.  Other than that I like it because it has nice tones and great exposure and the lighting is not flat.</td>', 'aka young death? Great except for the finger touching his nose so it looks kind of odd, and the harsh shadow to the viewing left of his hand.  Other than that I like it because it has nice tones and great exposure and the lighting is not flat.', '2008-10-07 01:19:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996269, 726969, 23002, '<td valign="top">hahaha.  thanks I needed a chuckle.<br/> <br/>I think this would actually do pretty well if it were not for the garrish pink background.  The high setup of your light being almost straight above and almost in the middle gives pretty much "butterfly lighting"  (see the shadow under the nose)  Unfortunately that is not gong to help the few skin imperfections.  Great looking model with nice hair. :)</td>', 'hahaha.  thanks I needed a chuckle. I think this would actually do pretty well if it were not for the garrish pink background.  The high setup of your light being almost straight above and almost in the middle gives pretty much "butterfly lighting"  (see the shadow under the nose)  Unfortunately that is not gong to help the few skin imperfections.  Great looking model with nice hair. :)', '2008-10-07 01:22:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996270, 726122, 23002, '<td valign="top">ummm. not a studio portait.  wrong challenge perhaps?</td>', 'ummm. not a studio portait.  wrong challenge perhaps?', '2008-10-07 01:23:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996273, 727166, 23002, '<td valign="top">I know you were looking for a dramatic effect here and you got it.  I am just not so sure that a half of a floating head really works for me.  Even a half a stop of fill would have made this much more interesting to me.<br/> <br/>I hope it does well for you because it is certainly different then the rest, and that is not always a bad thing. :)</td>', 'I know you were looking for a dramatic effect here and you got it.  I am just not so sure that a half of a floating head really works for me.  Even a half a stop of fill would have made this much more interesting to me. I hope it does well for you because it is certainly different then the rest, and that is not always a bad thing. :)', '2008-10-07 01:25:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996276, 726888, 23002, '<td valign="top">Great idea.  I think that you need a monitor calibration though. The shot it totally green and unfortunately you can see the shadow behind her so she was not far enouogh away from the backdrop or the backdrop was not lit on it''s own.  You can also see dark corners at the top of the image where the backdrop was not lit.<br/> <br/>A good concept which does not quiet come to fruition.  good luck.</td>', 'Great idea.  I think that you need a monitor calibration though. The shot it totally green and unfortunately you can see the shadow behind her so she was not far enouogh away from the backdrop or the backdrop was not lit on it''s own.  You can also see dark corners at the top of the image where the backdrop was not lit. A good concept which does not quiet come to fruition.  good luck.', '2008-10-07 01:27:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996277, 725127, 23002, '<td valign="top">studio portrait??????????????</td>', 'studio portrait??????????????', '2008-10-07 01:27:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996281, 726766, 23002, '<td valign="top">I am glad to see that you decided to go ahead with the validation. :)  I would not have questioned it because I recognize you in the photo and know what you can do using camera alone.<br/> <br/>Good luck.</td>', 'I am glad to see that you decided to go ahead with the validation. :)  I would not have questioned it because I recognize you in the photo and know what you can do using camera alone. Good luck.', '2008-10-07 01:29:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996284, 726893, 23002, '<td valign="top">Wow, the same model as with the globe a couple pictures ago.  Must be a family member of the previous photog or a group shoot or something. :)<br/> <br/>The severe crop and the lack of sharpness hurt this photo.  Once again she is either too close to the background or the background needs to be evenly lit to avoid the problems you can see in it.<br/> <br/>Good luck.</td>', 'Wow, the same model as with the globe a couple pictures ago.  Must be a family member of the previous photog or a group shoot or something. :) The severe crop and the lack of sharpness hurt this photo.  Once again she is either too close to the background or the background needs to be evenly lit to avoid the problems you can see in it. Good luck.', '2008-10-07 01:31:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996286, 725900, 23002, '<td valign="top">no vote from me.  I like the oof books in the background and he has a nice expression.<br/> <br/> <br/>good luck Alain.</td>', 'no vote from me.  I like the oof books in the background and he has a nice expression.  good luck Alain.', '2008-10-07 01:32:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996289, 726976, 23002, '<td valign="top">A very pleasent photo of a little girl.  Unfortunately with the way she is leaning backwards and with the lack of more fill it causes her eyes and mouth to be very dark, and also a very strong shadow below her chin.  The outfit blends into the background so a backlight would have also helped this.<br/> <br/>You have a great little model here so you will lots more chances to improve.  Good luck.</td>', 'A very pleasent photo of a little girl.  Unfortunately with the way she is leaning backwards and with the lack of more fill it causes her eyes and mouth to be very dark, and also a very strong shadow below her chin.  The outfit blends into the background so a backlight would have also helped this. You have a great little model here so you will lots more chances to improve.  Good luck.', '2008-10-07 01:34:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996290, 725129, 23002, '<td valign="top">ummm..studio portrait?</td>', 'ummm..studio portrait?', '2008-10-07 01:35:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996293, 726868, 23002, '<td valign="top">It could use a bit more fill to keep the shadow side of the nose from going almost black, and it looks like your background light is spilling onto the side of your subject causing discolouration.  I am also not a fan of the crop off of the head.<br/> <br/>fix those things and it would have been a 10.  now it is a very nice 6.</td>', 'It could use a bit more fill to keep the shadow side of the nose from going almost black, and it looks like your background light is spilling onto the side of your subject causing discolouration.  I am also not a fan of the crop off of the head. fix those things and it would have been a 10.  now it is a very nice 6.', '2008-10-07 01:37:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996295, 726998, 23002, '<td valign="top">IMHO the lighting is a bit too severe and a fill/reflector would have really helped by giving some light on his dark side and give some depth to the instrument.  The wrinkled backdrop is a bit distracting, so maybe a lower f stop would have put that a bit more oof.  Overall a nice portrait with great skin tones and a perfect exposure. 7</td>', 'IMHO the lighting is a bit too severe and a fill/reflector would have really helped by giving some light on his dark side and give some depth to the instrument.  The wrinkled backdrop is a bit distracting, so maybe a lower f stop would have put that a bit more oof.  Overall a nice portrait with great skin tones and a perfect exposure. 7', '2008-10-07 01:39:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996296, 726038, 23002, '<td valign="top">Great lighting job here.  It is a shame about the crummy apple laptop he is holding. lmao 8</td>', 'Great lighting job here.  It is a shame about the crummy apple laptop he is holding. lmao 8', '2008-10-07 01:40:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996297, 727104, 23002, '<td valign="top">unfortunately this shot is way overexposed, to the point that trying to bring it back to normal has shifted all your skin tones horribly. A nice idea, but needs a re-shoot to fix this overexposure.</td>', 'unfortunately this shot is way overexposed, to the point that trying to bring it back to normal has shifted all your skin tones horribly. A nice idea, but needs a re-shoot to fix this overexposure.', '2008-10-07 01:41:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996299, 725858, 23002, '<td valign="top">If you are going to do an ultra closeup it is a good idea to so so with a longer lense so that the nose does not look extra huge like it does here.  Sorry but this one does not work for me at all.</td>', 'If you are going to do an ultra closeup it is a good idea to so so with a longer lense so that the nose does not look extra huge like it does here.  Sorry but this one does not work for me at all.', '2008-10-07 01:42:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996300, 726731, 23002, '<td valign="top">the real expensive violin would explain why he looks so tense and nervous perhaps?  To me the photo even though the lighting is ok just lacks some pop, like it is amost missing some tonal range for some reason.</td>', 'the real expensive violin would explain why he looks so tense and nervous perhaps?  To me the photo even though the lighting is ok just lacks some pop, like it is amost missing some tonal range for some reason.', '2008-10-07 01:44:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996303, 725764, 23002, '<td valign="top">A nice little model you have there. :)<br/> <br/>The main issue I have with this shot is the severe craning of her neck to face the camera.  She is totally sideways to the camera.  Try her at a 45% instead. Seems slightly overexposed as well.  Fix those two things and you have a winner. :)</td>', 'A nice little model you have there. :) The main issue I have with this shot is the severe craning of her neck to face the camera.  She is totally sideways to the camera.  Try her at a 45% instead. Seems slightly overexposed as well.  Fix those two things and you have a winner. :)', '2008-10-07 01:46:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996308, 726408, 23002, '<td valign="top">If she was a bit farther from the background to get rid of that shadow it would be a very nice portrait of this little girl.  Also watch the cropping of the head, either make sure it looks like it was on purpose or do not do it at all.  Is there a reason why you took this as a horizontal instead of a verticle shot?  I think the extra space fights for the viewer''s attention at the sides.<br/> <br/>Overall a nice rendering of her which would have been much better with a couple of adjustments. :)<br/> <br/>Good luck.</td>', 'If she was a bit farther from the background to get rid of that shadow it would be a very nice portrait of this little girl.  Also watch the cropping of the head, either make sure it looks like it was on purpose or do not do it at all.  Is there a reason why you took this as a horizontal instead of a verticle shot?  I think the extra space fights for the viewer''s attention at the sides. Overall a nice rendering of her which would have been much better with a couple of adjustments. :) Good luck.', '2008-10-07 01:49:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996310, 726552, 23002, '<td valign="top">If only the background was not totally distracting this would be a really nice portrait of this nice young lady.  Everything else about it I like.</td>', 'If only the background was not totally distracting this would be a really nice portrait of this nice young lady.  Everything else about it I like.', '2008-10-07 01:50:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996319, 727197, 23002, '<td valign="top">The lighing is very nice except that you have her facing in towards the main light instead of the fill.  This has the effect of making her face look thicker then it really is, and is not condusive to a portrait of a little girl.  She is also almost sideways to the camera which makes her body look a bit distorted as well as means that for her to look at the camera her eyes are in the corners of the sockets so there is too much white on one side and none on the other sides.  I am also interested in why you chose a horizontal composition and cut off her head instead of a simple verticle one with all of her head?  This does nothing to add to the photo.  <br/> <br/>I love your background light in this, it is very effective.  She is a great little model and overall this is a pleasant photo, but was very close to being outstanding.<br/> <br/>Good luck.</td>', 'The lighing is very nice except that you have her facing in towards the main light instead of the fill.  This has the effect of making her face look thicker then it really is, and is not condusive to a portrait of a little girl.  She is also almost sideways to the camera which makes her body look a bit distorted as well as means that for her to look at the camera her eyes are in the corners of the sockets so there is too much white on one side and none on the other sides.  I am also interested in why you chose a horizontal composition and cut off her head instead of a simple verticle one with all of her head?  This does nothing to add to the photo.   I love your background light in this, it is very effective.  She is a great little model and overall this is a pleasant photo, but was very close to being outstanding. Good luck.', '2008-10-07 01:54:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996323, 726186, 23002, '<td valign="top">A very pleasant self portrait.  I am not crazy about the background colour though.  Is that you Dr. Phil???</td>', 'A very pleasant self portrait.  I am not crazy about the background colour though.  Is that you Dr. Phil???', '2008-10-07 01:55:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996324, 724927, 23002, '<td valign="top">The skin tones are very grey and non lifelike, and she does not appear to be in a studio??</td>', 'The skin tones are very grey and non lifelike, and she does not appear to be in a studio??', '2008-10-07 01:56:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996386, 726766, 97225, '<td valign="top">That''s cool, although the lighting may be a liitle harsh. I hope you tell us how you did this.</td>', 'That''s cool, although the lighting may be a liitle harsh. I hope you tell us how you did this.', '2008-10-07 03:34:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996463, 726491, 48228, '<td valign="top"><b>A</b> for Attitude <br/><b>W</b> for Well I <b>NEVER</b> <br/><b>E</b> for Ego<br/><b>S</b> for Special<br/><b>O</b> for Oh! my God<br/><b>M</b> for Mushy<br/><b>E</b> for Everything in the above photo makes me laugh.....<br/> <br/>What great candid.....</td>', 'A for Attitude W for Well I NEVER E for EgoS for SpecialO for Oh! my GodM for MushyE for Everything in the above photo makes me laugh..... What great candid.....', '2008-10-07 05:55:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996474, 726337, 95579, '<td valign="top">I like the grainyness to the background, it works well with the weathered face n cap</td>', 'I like the grainyness to the background, it works well with the weathered face n cap', '2008-10-07 06:22:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996567, 726161, 32011, '<td valign="top">Tatiana... that''s my daughters name  :)<br/> <br/>I know someone else on DPC that has a daughter with that name, and that someone happens to be on the Australian team for DPCO3... so, I''ll not vote on this, just incase this happens to be her entry.  :)<br/> <br/>Though, I''d like to comment.  Great photo.  Well composed and the colours are fantastic.  I''m really draw to the eyes, which is what you want... though, I''m not sure about the reflections in them... they''re a little distracting.  Other than that and the stray strand of hair on the cheek, I can''t really fault this.  I would have given this a 8, had I not excluded myself from voting.  :)</td>', 'Tatiana... that''s my daughters name  :) I know someone else on DPC that has a daughter with that name, and that someone happens to be on the Australian team for DPCO3... so, I''ll not vote on this, just incase this happens to be her entry.  :) Though, I''d like to comment.  Great photo.  Well composed and the colours are fantastic.  I''m really draw to the eyes, which is what you want... though, I''m not sure about the reflections in them... they''re a little distracting.  Other than that and the stray strand of hair on the cheek, I can''t really fault this.  I would have given this a 8, had I not excluded myself from voting.  :)', '2008-10-07 09:48:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996765, 725888, 99155, '<td valign="top">I like the action and the energy.</td>', 'I like the action and the energy.', '2008-10-07 12:32:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(4996857, 725984, 96915, '<td valign="top">Would have liked her eyes more in focus.  It appears that the tree is more in focus than the model.</td>', 'Would have liked her eyes more in focus.  It appears that the tree is more in focus than the model.', '2008-10-07 13:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
