(5065120, 726780, 13390, '<td valign="top">Glad to see you experimenting around with light, I need to do more of this. Even though I am no lighting expert by any stretch of the imagination, I''ll try to tell you what I see. I think you''re definitely on the right track. The light feels a little on the bright side and seems to fill every aspect of the shot, I think that''s where you''re using losing some detail. I can tell that there is some softness to the light which helps give that image some POP to it. Again, you''re already blazing trails I haven''t dared step into yet and I commend you for it. Just keep trying different situations and experimenting with the light and see what different results you get. Nicely done! Maybe try different WB in RAW as well.</td>', 'Glad to see you experimenting around with light, I need to do more of this. Even though I am no lighting expert by any stretch of the imagination, I''ll try to tell you what I see. I think you''re definitely on the right track. The light feels a little on the bright side and seems to fill every aspect of the shot, I think that''s where you''re using losing some detail. I can tell that there is some softness to the light which helps give that image some POP to it. Again, you''re already blazing trails I haven''t dared step into yet and I commend you for it. Just keep trying different situations and experimenting with the light and see what different results you get. Nicely done! Maybe try different WB in RAW as well.', '2008-11-15 13:07:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5069989, 726003, 39427, '<td valign="top">This is a very nice shot and has a lot going for it, including the lighting, unique angle and the pose.  However, the focus is a tad soft, and needs to be tack sharp on portraits (unless it is intentionally out of focus).  The eye is the focal point and it is blurry.  And I think it is a bit overexposed on the face, even given the "high-key" feel.  Finally, I think the photo could be improved with a contrast boost.  In remedying the exposure/contrast aspects of this image, you may need to do some form of selective adjustments on the left vs. the right side of the face because of the difference in values on either side.  Hope all these comments don''t come off as too negative, I just really like the shot and thought I would offer some criticism</td>', 'This is a very nice shot and has a lot going for it, including the lighting, unique angle and the pose.  However, the focus is a tad soft, and needs to be tack sharp on portraits (unless it is intentionally out of focus).  The eye is the focal point and it is blurry.  And I think it is a bit overexposed on the face, even given the "high-key" feel.  Finally, I think the photo could be improved with a contrast boost.  In remedying the exposure/contrast aspects of this image, you may need to do some form of selective adjustments on the left vs. the right side of the face because of the difference in values on either side.  Hope all these comments don''t come off as too negative, I just really like the shot and thought I would offer some criticism', '2008-11-18 19:12:28.000000', NULL, 0),
